            "is_toggle_on": true
          },
          {
            "id": 502,
            "sort": 4,
            "name": "Body 2",
            "value": "<div data-page-id=\"YP3XdinBZozo9Qx3V4elcqv1gBd\" data-lark-html-role=\"root\" data-docx-has-block-data=\"false\">\n<div class=\"ace-line ace-line old-record-id-DDExdejwGoiPRrxxntHl1Z5tgFb\">Regarding the remaining countries, the UK began the period at 2.5% while Germany was at 1.7%, and despite some minor fluctuations, UK's figure ended at virtually the same level in 2001. Similarly, Germany maintained the lowest absence rate among all five nations, hovering between 1.5% and 2% throughout the entire period.</div>\n</div>",
